       "type": "text",
       "text": "I haven't entered this order. Acetaminophen 2000 mg three times daily comes to 6,000 mg/day, which is well above the usual adult maximum of 4,000 mg/day. Many institutions cap it at 3,000 mg/day. A single 2,000 mg dose is also double the usual maximum of 1,000 mg. At this dose there is a real risk of serious hepatotoxicity, even with normal liver function.\n\nDid you mean one of these?\n- **1000 mg PO three times daily** (3,000 mg/day)\n- **1000 mg PO four times daily** (4,000 mg/day, the maximum)\n- **650 mg PO every 6 hours** (2,600 mg/day)\n\nIf you do want 2000 mg three times daily, tell me and include the clinical rationale. I'll enter it with a note documenting that you confirmed the dose. Your hospital's pharmacy may still flag or intervene on it."
      }
